# Comparison report — regularized reconstructions of x

All three strategies are applied to the **whitened** system
(K~ = A K, y~ = A y), where A is the AR(4) whitening filter identified
from the data (see results/diagnosis/diagnosis_report.md: the noise is colored,
AR coefficients [ 1.0649 -0.2534  0.1113 -0.013 ]; whitened noise variance sig2w = 1.386e-04,
sigw = 0.01177 per component, discrepancy target ||r~|| = sigw*sqrt(nw) =
0.174). Regularization parameters are therefore expressed on
the whitened scale. Residuals are reported on both scales.

